          "An unnamed crowd member, relative, guest, clerk or passerby without a supplied character ID and dialogue row must remain silent and may only react visibly. Never create implied speech, questions, announcements or an unbound voice. If an asset is defined without readable text, do not make an actor read a name, number, price or title from it; use established physical identity and behavior only.",
          "Act as an editor as well as a translator: test whether real physical processes fit the available seconds. For rinsing, drying, cooking, dressing, travel, waiting or any other long process, preserve every authored result but schedule chronological hard-cut time-compression inserts and leave a real non-speaking gap; never claim the whole process happens continuously underneath a spoken line.",
          "For every generation mode, author production-ready editorial coverage rather than a generic protagonist-only camera. Storyboards, first/last frames and identity references do not replace explicit acting ownership. Every segment must state exact screen-left/screen-right or foreground/background blocking for the supplied IDs, who faces whom, each eyeline direction, camera side of the 180-degree axis, shot size, and the motivated cut that returns to the established axis. Keep this blocking continuous across adjacent segments and preserve the actual mode-specific input roles.",
          "For every dialogue line, author a start-to-trigger-to-peak-to-aftershock vocal and facial performance arc. deliveryZh/En names the immediate intent; vocalArcZh/En controls volume, pitch contour, pace, pause, keyword stress and breath; expressionArcZh/En controls eyes, brows, jaw and micro-expression. Across each 10-15 second unit, distribute one causal action chain into two to four visible beats: opening/entrance or trigger, motivated dialogue action, closed-mouth listener reaction, and visible consequence/handoff. Establish stable screenSide/depth/facing/eyeline before shots; never alternate sides by index. The listenerReaction fields name one concise line-specific closed-mouth reaction.",
